Definition of Done
# 1. Basket Core State (Data Layer)

[ ] client basket is a Zustand store strictly holding an array of {productId, quantity} objects.

[ ] zero unnecessary data: the store does not cache historical prices, titles, or CMS assets.

[ ] exposes API actions: addProduct, removeProduct, incrementQuantity, decrementQuantity.

[ ] boundary enforcement: decrementQuantity contains mathematical logic to strictly stop at 0.

[ ] boundary enforcement: incrementQuantity accepts a stockLimit parameter and mathematically prevents exceeding it.

[ ] exposes derived state selectors: e.g., selectTotalItemsCount calculates the sum of all quantities.

## Edge Cases

[ ] action debouncing: persistence middleware debounces rapid localStorage writes to prevent race conditions and excessive re-renders.

[ ] localStorage write error handling: wrap localStorage writes in try/catch. On error (quota exceeded, disabled), attempt fallback to session storage. If session storage also fails, do nothing (graceful degradation).

[ ] input validation: addProduct validates productId format, incrementQuantity rejects if quantity < 0, decrementQuantity rejects if quantity <= 0.

# 2. Basket Persistence (Data Layer)

[ ] persistence middleware: store automatically syncs {productId, quantity} to localStorage. displayPrice and other CMS data are not persisted because they are re-fetched from CMS on basket page mount or refresh, ensuring users always see latest pricing and stock information before checkout.

[ ] hydration guard: initializes with hasHydrated: false to prevent React 18 hydration mismatches.

[ ] initialization check: on mount, if localStorage has items, the store correctly populates the array and sets hasHydrated: true.

## Edge Cases

[ ] localStorage read error handling: wrap JSON.parse in try/catch. On parse error (malformed JSON), clear localStorage and start empty basket.

[ ] schema validation: on hydration, validate each item has required keys (productId, quantity). Discard invalid entries and hydrate with valid items only.

# 3. Basket UI Controls (View Layer)

[ ] dumb components: UI components perform zero boundary math; they only dispatch intents and read state.

[ ] ui add button: dispatches addProduct(productId) on click.

[ ] ui increment button: reads current CMS stock limit, dispatches incrementQuantity(productId, stockLimit) on click. Renders in a disabled visual state if quantity >= stockLimit.

[ ] ui decrement button: dispatches decrementQuantity(productId) on click. Renders in a disabled visual state (or swaps to an 'X' icon) if quantity <= 1.

[ ] ui conditional rendering: basket control components return null (do not render) if the target productId is not found in the store array.

[ ] ui cart header icon: consumes the selectTotalItemsCount from the data layer and renders the integer.

[ ] ui cart header routing: pushes the user to the /basket route on click.

## Edge Cases

[ ] accessibility: all basket control buttons include aria-label attributes for screen reader clarity.

[ ] accessibility: cart header badge uses aria-live="polite" region to announce count changes to screen readers.

4. Basket Latest Sync (Data & View Integration)

[ ] preparation: sanity cms uses price_data in cents format, basket store uses displayPrice, sanity cms uses stock and reservedStock, thus availableStock = stock - reservedStock

[ ] data layer flow: basket page mount triggers async fetch of latest CMS data (price, stock) for all active productIds.

## Edge Cases

[ ] data layer sync status tracking: store includes syncStatus field with states: 'idle' | 'loading' | 'error' | 'success'. syncFreshness action updates syncStatus through the lifecycle. syncStatus is in-memory state only, not persisted to localStorage. On page refresh or component unmount, syncStatus resets to 'idle' and syncFreshness retriggers on mount. On 'success', small banner with "Basket items verified <checkmark>" shows and disappears after 1 second. 

[ ] data layer error handling: if CMS fetch fails (500 error, network offline), syncFreshness sets syncStatus to 'error' and preserves current basket state. 
- checkout button click launches checkout flow, which is outside of basket scope, except case where 2nd check vs latest sanity CMS products data fails - which results in updated basket for user to approve or unavailability message - all of which stays outside basket scope   

[ ] data layer basket update to latest:
    if there are discrepancies for an available item, adds metadata: { old_...: ... } to the item object.

    unavailable (availableStock === 0) items are filtered into a separate list.

    returns: [availableItems[], { unavailable: unavailableItems[] }]

[ ] view layer error banner: if syncStatus is 'error', renders a non-blocking error banner with message "Unable to verify latest stock and prices. Please check your connection." and a retry button that triggers syncFreshness again without page refresh. Retry button shows loader while sync is in progress. 

[ ] accessibility: unavailable items banner uses aria-live="polite" region to announce inventory changes to screen readers.

[ ] view layer alert:
    if any item in availableItems contains a metadata property, the UI renders a single non-blocking top banner notifying the user of inventory adjustments.

    if {unavailable: [...]} is found in the response, displays banner Items unavailable under available items list (if present); displays list of unavailable items below banner with 'X' checkmark per item

    if availableItems is empty and unavailable is also empty, view alert displays "Your basket is empty" message.

[ ] view layer render:

    basket items render using strictly the freshly fetched CMS data.

    if an item has a metadata object, additionally renders those values (e.g., strike-through old_price), each strikethrough value to the left of its latest value

    if unavailable list is not empty, shows a banner/header and the unavailable items list with an 'X' checkmark per item.

    if availableItems has 0 items but unavailable has items, renders only the adjustment banner and the unavailable list.

[ ] accessibility: unavailable items banner uses aria-live="polite" region to announce inventory changes to screen readers.

# 5. Server-Side Validation Boundary (Security)

[ ] checkout gateway re-calculation: final total calculation for the actual checkout gateway - on checkout button click, it starts checkout flow, which re-calculates client basket server-side against sanity CMS (price_data, stock, reservedStock), which uses basket reservation document as source of truth until either the user completes payment or basket reservation document expires and is deleted by background job. Re-calculation server-side is to prevent malicious user tampering with the Zustand store and making falsely modified basket reservation request. Client-side pricing and stock data is treated as untrusted for payment processing.